comments.body:
Perhaps less ergonomic, but consistent with your choice for not supporting `*args`. Anyway, I prefer to have `**kwargs` rather than nothing :-p

Apart from this, and going back to your previous message in which you said "_the ergonomic downside with *args style is passing in an existing (or programmatically-generated) list of expressions into the method;_", what about supporting all these uses cases? For example: 
```
def with_columns(self, *args, **kwargs):
  if len(args) == 1:
    if isinstance(args[0], list):
      args = args[0]
   ...
```
